-- title:
--   Tree-lattice facts for the even part of a Čerednik–Drinfeld group
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$ and a commutative domain $\mathcal O$ of characteristic zero which is a discrete valuation ring, together with an irreducible element $\pi$ such that $\mathcal O$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete, $\#(\mathcal O/(\pi)) = r$ and $(r) = (\pi)$; let $K_0$ be a characteristic-zero field realised as the fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Let $vdet : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) satisfy: $vdet(g) = n$ exactly when $\det g = u\,\pi^n$ in $K_0$ for some $u \in \mathcal O^\times$. Let $G$ be a group, $\sigma : G \to \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and $\rho : G \to \mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ the homomorphism obtained by composing $\sigma$ with the projection, and let $\Gamma \le G$ contain an element $z$ with $\sigma z$ a scalar matrix and $vdet(\sigma z) = 2$, and an element $w$ with $vdet(\sigma w) = 1$. Let $\Gamma' \le G$ be characterised by $x \in \Gamma'$ iff $x \in \Gamma$ and $vdet(\sigma x)$ is even. Assume that on the Bruhat–Tits tree, whose vertices are homothety classes of full $\mathcal O$-lattices in $K_0^2$ with adjacency generated by the relation $\mathrm{AdjacentLattice}$, the image $\rho(\Gamma')$ has finite vertex stabilisers and admits a finite set $S$ of vertices meeting every $\rho(\Gamma')$-orbit. The conclusion asserts: $\rho(\Gamma')$ lies in the type-preserving subgroup for the standard vertex $[\mathcal O^2]$, i.e. the elements fixing the parity of the graph distance to $[\mathcal O^2]$; $\rho(\Gamma')$ acts by graph automorphisms (adjacency is preserved), with finite dart stabilisers and finitely many orbits of vertices and of darts; some $\gamma \in \Gamma$ has $\rho(\gamma)$ not type-preserving; for $x \in \Gamma$, membership in $\Gamma'$ is equivalent to $\rho(x)$ being type-preserving; the same graph-action, finite-dart-stabiliser and finite-orbit-quotient statements hold for $\rho(\Gamma)$; and the relative index of $\Gamma'$ in $\Gamma$ is nonzero.
--
--   This collects the discreteness, cocompactness and type-preservation data needed to apply Mumford-style quotient-graph arguments to a Čerednik–Drinfeld group acting on the Bruhat–Tits tree of $\mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$, isolating the even part $\Gamma'$ as exactly the part acting without interchanging the two vertex types. It feeds the later construction of the invariant ring and of the function field of the quotient in the $p$-adic uniformisation of Shimura curves.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_map_evenPart_le_typePreserving_and_graphAction_and_finite_of_cerednikDrinfeld_group.lean

